      "page_idx": 18,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.083,
            0.743,
            0.141
          ],
          "content": "The water vapour in the air condenses to form tiny droplets of water, which appear as clouds. Many tiny water droplets come together and fall down as rain, hail or snow."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.147,
            0.742,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": " The circulation of water between the Earth surface and atmosphere is known as the water cycle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.19,
            0.743,
            0.249
          ],
          "content": "We have used the process of observation, questioning, possible reason and experimenting to find out the concepts of evaporation and condensation."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.287,
            0.6,
            0.311
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Let us enhance our learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.611,
            0.25,
            0.735,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.349,
            0.742,
            0.478
          ],
          "content": "1. Which of the following best describes condensation? (i) The conversion of water into its vapour state. (ii) The process of water changing from a liquid into gaseous state. (iii) The formation of clouds from tiny water droplets. (iv) The conversion of water vapour into its liquid state."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.484,
            0.743,
            0.522
          ],
          "content": "2. Identify in which of the given processes, evaporation is very important—"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.531,
            0.601,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "(i) Colouring with (a) crayons (b) water colours (c) acrylic colours (d) pencil colours"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.603,
            0.727,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Writing on paper with (a) pencil (b) ink pen (c) ball point pen"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.653,
            0.743,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "3. We see green coloured plastic grass at many places these days. Space around natural grass feels cooler than space around the plastic grass. Can you find out why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.718,
            0.726,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "4. Give examples of liquids other than water that evaporate."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.747,
            0.743,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": "5. Fans move air around, creating a cooling sensation. It might seem strange to use a fan to dry wet clothes since fans usually make things cooler, not warmer. Normally, when water evaporates, it requires heat, not cold air. What do you think about this?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.848,
            0.744,
            0.906
          ],
          "content": "6. Usually, when sludge is removed from drains, it is left in heaps next to the drain for 3–4 days. Afterward, it is transported to a garden or a field where it can be used as"
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
            0.888,
            0.697,
            0.91,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": "A Journey through States of Water"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
